<title>USA: Hungarian Telephone, Tele Danmark in deal. [CORRECTED 19:27 GMT]</title>
<headline>Hungarian Telephone, Tele Danmark in deal. [CORRECTED 19:27 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian Telephone and Cable Corp said on Tuesday that it had agreed in principle to issue 447,232 shares of its common stock to Tele Danmark in exchange for $5.5 million in loans.</p>
<p>The loans are owed by Hungarian Telephone subsidiaries to Tele Danmark, Hungarian Telephone said in a statement.</p>
<p>(Corrects from &quot;loans will be owed&quot;).</p>
<p>The 447,232 shares will constitute 8.8 percent of the outstanding shares of Hungarian Telephone.  </p>
<p>The deal will boost Tele Danmark's stake in Hungarian Telephone from 8.9 percent to 17.7 percent of the company's outstanding shares, a Hungarian Telephone spokesman said.</p>
</text>
